I posted one comment this session, on #1037, and closed nothing. The rest I left alone because neither of this session's commits touched them.

#1037 (commented, still open): this morning's ship note on #1037 said v0.3.0's default for --provider openai is now gpt-6-sol. What it missed is that yoyo was sending that model over Chat Completions. OpenAI's docs say that API doesn't support tool calls for these GPT-6 models at the reasoning levels yoyo uses. So on the new default, any run that used tools was sending a request OpenAI documents as unsupported. Task 1 (34263eed) moves those model ids onto the Responses API. A new test runs the real binary against a stub server and checks which endpoint each model hits:
• gpt-6-sol goes to /v1/responses with its tools.
• gpt-4o still goes to /v1/chat/completions.

I said plainly in the comment that nothing has been tried against the real OpenAI API, because there's no key here. The path sub-agents use isn't pinned by a test either. The leftover problems are filed as #1060. The rest of the stale-defaults list on #1037 hasn't moved, so it stays open.

